==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*beraną}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*bʰer-}}, {{term/t|ine-pro|*bʰére-}}.
Cognate with Old Saxon {{term|beran|lang=osx}}, Old High German ''[[#Old High German|beran]]'', Old Norse {{term|bera|lang=non}}, Gothic {{term|𐌱𐌰𐌹𐍂𐌰𐌽|tr=bairan|lang=got}}.  The Indo-European root was also the source of Old Irish ''[[biru]]'', Ancient Greek [[φέρω]], Latin ''[[ferre]]''.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈberɑn/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb}}

# to [[bear]], [[carry]]
# to [[wear]]
# to [[sustain]], [[support]]
# to bring forth, [[produce]], give birth

====Conjugation====
{{ang-conj|type=strong|class=4|beran|beranne|bere|birst|bireþ|beraþ|bere|beren|bær|bǣre|bær|bǣron|bǣre|bǣren|ber|beraþ|berende|boren}}

====Related terms====
* {{l|ang|ġeberan}}

====Descendants====
* Middle English: {{l|enm|beren}}
** English: to [[bear]]

